ubi: guard ubi_find_volume() against an unattached UBI device

ubi_find_volume() loops `ubi->vtbl_slots` with no check that a UBI partition is
attached. When `ubi` is NULL (no `ubi part` has run) the loop walks a garbage
device and strcmp()s a bad volume-name pointer -> Synchronous Abort.

This bites the Airoha EN8811H PHY's FW_IN_UBI path: it calls ubi_volume_read()
during `Net:` init, before anything attached the UBI. With env in UBI the env
load happened to attach it first; with CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE (r3-mini provisioning
u-boot) nothing attaches it, so the en8811h fw read crashed u-boot before it
reached the prompt.

Return NULL when no device is attached; ubi_volume_read() then returns ENODEV and
the caller (en8811h) skips gracefully. Generic, harmless robustness fix.
--- a/cmd/ubi.c
+++ b/cmd/ubi.c
@@ -256,6 +256,9 @@
 	struct ubi_volume *vol;
 	int i;
 
+	if (!ubi)
+		return NULL;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < ubi->vtbl_slots; i++) {
 		vol = ubi->volumes[i];
 		if (vol && !strcmp(vol->name, volume))
